  "summary": "Seven preprints in one week pair open software with QC benchmarks across MS imaging, lipidomics, metabolomics, and low-input and single-cell proteomics.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is the standardization of mass spectrometry data handling, with most items offering software or benchmarks for quality control and interpretation. Several are R Shiny applications: LipidRT uses retention time coherence to validate and expand lipid annotations, OSMSS gives non-coders differential abundance, phosphosite and enrichment analyses, and MetaboRx combines quality metrics with preprocessing for metabolomics. msiFlow 2.0 adds mass recalibration, lipid annotation, batch correction and visual QC to an imaging pipeline. QC Shotgun defines eight relative metrics for instrument performance in shotgun lipidomics. Sample-limited proteomics is addressed by a NanoShield trap column benchmark against PepMap and direct injection, and by SCP-Viz, a visual toolkit for single-cell data. The emphasis is on reproducibility, annotation reliability and usability rather than new acquisition principles.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-19"
}
